@page "/editor"
@inject NavigationManager Navigation

@* Whoever types /editor ends up on /editor/drawio. Nothing is drawn here.

   WHY A REDIRECT AND NOT A ROUTE TAKEN AWAY. Taking the route away was the other option, and it is
   worse for the one thing that matters at the beta: the address is out there. It is in the product
   itself (ImportExport.razor navigates to it after an import), it is in whatever anybody has
   bookmarked, and it is the address the WinForms era's Editor answered to. Without this component
   all of those land on the router's <NotFound>, which is the bare line "Pagina non trovata." - and
   somebody who typed the address he has always used, and got a blank page with four words on it,
   reads that as "the Editor is broken", not as "the Editor moved". A redirect answers the question
   he actually had.

   WHAT IT COSTS, AND WHY IT IS SAFE. This component declares NO render mode, so it is rendered
   statically: NavigateTo in OnInitialized is then an HTTP redirect issued by the server, and the
   old canvas (Editor.razor, which has no @page any more) is never instantiated - which is the
   point, because it took the edit permit as it opened and so kept draw.io from saving. Not being
   interactive is also what keeps it out of OnlyAllowlistedComponentsAreInteractiveTest's
   allowlist: it shows nothing of the plant, so there is nothing here to deny to whoever has no key.

   THE ADDRESS IT SENDS TO is inside /editor, so ApiKeyMiddleware lets it through by the same
   prefix that lets this page through: "/editor" in AnonymousPathPrefixes covers /editor/drawio as
   well. That prefix must not be narrowed to this page - doing so would lock out the new Editor,
   not the old one. *@

@code {
    /// <summary>
    /// The whole page. <c>replace: true</c> so the browser's Back button goes wherever the operator
    /// came from and not back onto this address, which would bounce him forward again and leave him
    /// unable to go back at all.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// <b>OnInitialized, and not OnAfterRender.</b> Static rendering never calls OnAfterRender, so
    /// moving this line there would turn <c>GET /editor</c> into a <c>200 OK</c> with an empty
    /// <c>Location</c> - a blank page - and bUnit would not notice, because bUnit DOES call
    /// OnAfterRender: measured on 2026-09-18, all 981 of <c>Wcs.WebEditor.Test</c> stayed green
    /// through that change.
    /// The only test that goes red is <c>Wcs.WebEditor.Browser.Test.EditorRouteRedirectTest</c>,
    /// against a real host.
    /// </remarks>
    protected override void OnInitialized() => Navigation.NavigateTo("/editor/drawio", replace: true);
}
